":"Standing still is a bad idea in this Y2K-styled arena movement shooter. You fight through robot drones sent by the mining corporation Tigris Nix, which wants to drain a natural force called the Love from your planet. Destroying its drones helps heal the Oasis.\n\nSpeed is the core mechanic, and moving fast is rewarded twice, since it raises both your damage and your healing. Wave hopping, dashes, double jumps and ground slams carry the movement, while weapons with secondary fire modes combine for layered effects and bigger Love scores. It draws on boomer shooters and suits single-player fans of fast, precise, high-skill shooting."}}